@startuml elm
title ELM v3: from student information to credentials

rectangle "Student records\n(Ladok, SIS)" as src
rectangle "ELM v3 student information\n--\nPerson (credentialSubject)\n  hasClaim: LearningAchievement\n    specifiedBy: Qualification / Specification\n    wasDerivedFrom: LearningAssessment (grade)\n    wasInfluencedBy: LearningActivity\n    awardedBy: Organisation\n    creditReceived (ECTS)" as elm
rectangle "European Digital Credential (EDC)\n--\nELM content\n+ W3C VC envelope:\n  @context, type, issuer,\n  issued, validFrom, credentialSchema" as edc
rectangle "Sealed EDC\n--\nJAdES:\n{ payload, signatures }" as sealed
rectangle "Micro-credential\n--\nan EDC whose claim fills\nall Annex I fields\n(ECTS, EQF level, outcomes,\nassessment, participation, QA)" as mc

src --> elm
elm --> edc : wrap in VC envelope
edc --> sealed : EDCI seals
edc ..> mc : if Annex I complete

note bottom of elm
  ELM profiles that are not about a learner
  (LOQ: learning opportunities and qualifications,
   AMS: accreditation) describe catalogues and
  institutions, not student information.
end note

note right of edc
  SIS /api/v1/parse and /populate accept the
  plain, {"credential": ...} and sealed shapes
  and map the ELM content to Edu-API / OEAPI.
end note
@enduml
